🚨 **BLOCKING: the `@Skip` annotation is inert — the group still runs and will break test collection**

`package:test` only honors `@Skip` when attached to `test()`/`group()`/`main` — as metadata on a plain helper function it does nothing (verified with a minimal probe: an `@Skip`'d helper's group executed and failed). Run the suite on this branch and you can see it: the two `factory/teammate.yml leg runner` tests are listed as ✅ passing, not ⏭️ skipped — only `factory_stub_ref_test.dart`'s `skip:`-parameter test is actually skipped.

Consequences:

1. The documented skip does not exist — CI keeps executing the leg-runner contract against the in-tree submodule copy that no longer receives any calls (the stub now calls `dmtools-agentic-workflows@b93dc51`).
2. At exactly the follow-up this skip documents (dmtools-agents#591 retires the copy + submodule bump), the group body's `_read(_teammateFactoryPath)` runs at **test collection time** (group bodies execute even for skipped groups) and its `fail('missing expected file: …')` will error the whole suite — the moment the skip is supposed to protect is the moment the suite breaks.

Fix (keeps registration safe forever):

```dart
void _teammateFactoryContract() {
  // Re-home to the dmtools-agentic-workflows pin as a follow-up (#591).
  if (!File(_teammateFactoryPath).existsSync()) return;
  group('factory/teammate.yml leg runner', skip: 'pending dmtools-agents#591', () {
    final yaml = _read(_teammateFactoryPath);
    ...
```

(or guard the `_teammateFactoryContract()` call site in `main()` with the same `existsSync()` check). CI checks out submodules (`quality.yml` `submodules: true`), so the file exists today and the failure only fires after the bump — but this PR is what sets up that bump path.

