⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the freeze-model doc comments in both test files now contradict the code**

This PR changes the contract that the library-level docs still define — the docs were left on the old model:

- `factory_stub_ref_test.dart:6-16` still says: *"`ai-teammate.yml` still calls the historical factory-teammate.yml inside the `agents` submodule pin (teammate migration is a follow-up) — there the old in-lockstep contract holds: uses-SHA == submodule gitlink == the factory_ref input."* The new `_teammateLockstepPin` (this hunk) implements the opposite: uses-SHA = factory-home pin (dmtools-agentic-workflows), `factory_ref` = submodule gitlink, and the two SHAs are now deliberately **different**.
- `machine_sm_watchdog_test.dart:11-19` still says: *"Only the teammate leg still calls the historical factory inside the agents submodule (its migration is a follow-up), so its factory contract groups keep reading the in-tree submodule copy"* — the leg now calls the AW home and that group is (meant to be) skipped, not kept.

These headers are the spec the next maintainer reads before touching a pin; right now each file carries two contradictory contracts. Please update both headers to the two-pin freeze model, e.g.:

```
/// - `ai-teammate.yml` calls the factory home (dmtools-agentic-workflows)
///   pinned to its own immutable SHA; the `agents` submodule gitlink rides
///   the factory_ref input as the ENGINE pin — the two pins are independent
///   and must never be conflated.
```

(Anchored here because the changed doc lines are the new half of the contradiction; the stale halves are lines 6-16 of this file and lines 3-19 of `machine_sm_watchdog_test.dart`.)

